# herdr plugin set — declared, not accumulated.
# Each entry replaces a capability retired with Atrium. `herdr-lazy sync`
# converges a machine to this list; the lockfile beside it pins commits.
#
# Deliberately NOT `herdr-lazy init` output: that writes a curated default
# bundle. This list is only what earned a place.

# Multi-account Claude: profiles, usage monitor, auto-switch fallback chain.
# Replaces Atrium's claude_accounts + pool round-robin.
uwuclxdy/clauth/herdr-plugin

# worktree.created hook: symlink node_modules et al, copy settings.local.json.
# Replaces Atrium's link_paths + carry_files. herdr's own worktree commands
# have no hook system, which is the entire gap this fills.
tdi/herdr-worktree-setup

# Orchestration substrate: hosts Claude Code's NATIVE agent teams as real
# herdr panes (teammux shim). Replaces Atrium's fan-out.
caioniehues/herdmates

# Auto-prompting. Replaces Atrium's autoyes daemon (which was OFF). DISABLED
# (2026-08-28, `herdr plugin disable` + `hap pause`): it runs a live daemon by
# default, not the shadow-mode-only behavior originally intended — re-enable
# only after confirming it stays observe-only. See ~/herdr-setup-review.md P0-4.
0xGosu/herdr-auto-pilot

# This manager itself. NOT on PATH by design (README §Use) and auto-sync is
# off, so a rebuild restores it only via:
#   herdr plugin install natori-hrj/herdr-lazy && herdr-lazy restore
# (the herdr-lazy() shell function in zshrc.company resolves the binary path).
natori-hrj/herdr-lazy

# Diff review sidebar — the Atrium DIFF/review loop had no herdr equivalent
# until this. Added 2026-08-29 per herdr-setup-review.md P3.
persiyanov/herdr-reviewr

# Ticket -> worktree: files a herdr worktree from a Linear ticket, firing the
# same worktree.created steps as any other worktree (tdi.worktree-setup).
# Needs LINEAR_API_KEY in the server env to actually reach Linear. Added
# 2026-08-29 per herdr-setup-review.md P3.
tdi/herdr-worktree-from-linear

# Publishes a `$pr` token on the focused agent pane, so the open pull request
# for that worktree's branch shows up in the sidebar row instead of needing a
# `gh pr view`. Added 2026-08-29 per the herdr optimization pass (decision 7).
wyattjoh/herdr-plugin-gh-pr
